<section>
	<h2 id="proteusthemes-options">ProteusThemes Options</h2>
	<p>Open <b>Appearance &gt; Customize &gt; [PT] Theme Options</b> to preview and change the theme settings, then publish your changes.</p>
	<p>The available sections are:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><b>Logo</b></li>
		<li><b>Header &amp; Breadcrumbs</b></li>
		<li><b>Navigation</b></li>
		<li><b>Main Title Area</b></li>
		<li><b>Fonts</b></li>
		<li><b>Theme Layout &amp; Colors</b></li>
		<li><b>Projects</b></li>
		<li><b>Shop (with WooCommerce)</b></li>
		<li><b>Page Builder Row Styles</b></li>
		<li><b>Footer</b></li>
		<li><b>Custom Code</b></li>
		<li><b>Other</b></li>
	</ul>
	<p>Set the favicon using <b>Appearance &gt; Customize &gt; Site Identity &gt; Site Icon</b>.</p>
	<h3 id="google-maps-api-key">Google Maps API Key</h3>
	<p>Before using the Google Map widget, follow <a href="https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/javascript/get-api-key" target="_blank">Google's Maps JavaScript API setup instructions</a> to enable the API, configure billing and create a key restricted to your website. Enter it in <b>Appearance &gt; Customize &gt; [PT] Theme Options &gt; Other &gt; Google maps API key</b> and publish the change.</p>
	<p>Then add the Google Map widget in Page Builder or a widget area, set the map center and location coordinates, and adjust the zoom and height.</p>
</section>
